# Step-by-step: Flash using UNO as USB-serial (no FTDI)
1. Install ESP8266 board support in Arduino IDE.  
2. Remove the ATmega328P from UNO or press RESET on UNO so it doesn’t interfere.  
3. Wire as above (UNO TX→ESP RX, UNO RX→ESP TX, common GND, external 3.3V power).  
4. Put ESP into flash mode: connect **GPIO0 → GND** (and keep GPIO2 pulled HIGH to 3.3V).  
5. Power the ESP (or press RST).  
6. In Arduino IDE select board + COM port (the UNO’s USB serial shows).  
7. Upload sketch. If upload fails: try pressing and holding the ESP RST or re-power while hitting Upload.  
8. After successful upload, remove GPIO0 from GND and reset to boot normally.

If you used an FTDI adapter instead, you usually only need to pull GPIO0 to GND and press reset to flash.

